From: Flux LTP compatibility work
Subject: [PATCH] sched: disable MM CID allocation for Flux

Flux preserves the base rseq ABI, but its library-OS task/MM lifecycle does
not support the scheduler MM CID delayed-work optimization safely.  Keep the
existing CPU-ID fallback for rseq mm_cid and avoid stale dynamic-percpu state.

diff --git a/kernel/init/Kconfig b/kernel/init/Kconfig
--- a/kernel/init/Kconfig
+++ b/kernel/init/Kconfig
@@ -1016,6 +1016,6 @@ endif #CGROUP_SCHED
 
 config SCHED_MM_CID
 	def_bool y
-	depends on SMP && RSEQ
+	depends on SMP && RSEQ && !FLUX
 
 config UCLAMP_TASK_GROUP
